        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la nevera",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la nevera — \"the fridge\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "La nevera está casi vacía. The fridge is almost empty."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "El frigorífico is also common in Spain; in parts of Latin America people say el refrigerador or la heladera."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nevera comes from Latin nivārius 'of snow' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), built on nix, nivis 'snow', which also gave nieve. It was first a place where snow was stored to keep things cold."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
